  "reason": "Both completed experiments (config_004, config_036) used avgpool aggregation and achieved ~0.635–0.639 accuracy. The only difference between them was the image encoder (resnet50 slightly better), which is a small gap. The largest untested design dimension for multiprofile settings is the aggregation method: transformer aggregation can model inter-profile dependencies that avgpool discards. config_013 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while keeping the otherwise-best settings (pca_n2000, resnet50, weighted fusion), making it a clean single-variable test. This is the highest-uncertainty, highest-impact choice: if transformer aggregation helps, it could unlock meaningful accuracy gains across many downstream configs; if it doesn't, we confirm avgpool suffices and can focus remaining budget on other axes (RNA encoder, fusion). Expected cost: transformer attention over multiple profiles adds overhead on top of config_036's 10.60 GPU-hr baseline, so I estimate ~13–15 GPU hours—moderately more expensive but justified by the potential accuracy lift and the information gained for the remaining 6 experiments."
}

